armacraft perf patch 0001 -- UNAPPLIED. Render at START_SERVER_TICK instead of END_SERVER_TICK.

Why: in Minecraft 26.3 entity changes go out from ChunkMap.tick() (ServerEntity.sendChanges), which
runs inside ServerLevel.tick -> ServerChunkCache.tick. Fabric's START_SERVER_TICK is injected right
before MinecraftServer.tickChildren (so before the level tick); END_SERVER_TICK is at the TAIL of
tickServer (after it). The controller renders at END, so every snapTo / setTransformation made in
tick N is only picked up by ChunkMap.tick in tick N+1: one extra tick (50 ms) on every
snapshot -> client hop, for cycles, walls, names and the chase cam alike.

Effect (estimated from code, not measured in a running server): -50 ms on all visual latency.
Risk: low. Input handling (mixin) is untouched. Anything that relied on "render happened after the
level tick" (nothing found in host/src) would see the update one tick earlier, not later.

Base: host/src/main/java/gl/syn/armacraft/Armacraft.java as of 2026-10-02 00:05 BST.
Checked: `git apply --check` against the working tree; host main + test + gametest sources compile
with it (javac against the loom/Gradle cache jars). Not run in a server.
Apply from the repo root:  git apply docs/perf-patches/0001-host-render-at-tick-start.patch
(host/ files are CRLF; the patch carries CRLF context lines.)

